@startuml STM-4
!include _style.iuml
title STM-4 (System level) — Lifecycle of a TopUp\ntop_ups.status · v1.2 · 23/11/2026

state c1 <<choice>>
[*] --> pending : / send payment request
note left of pending
  created when the Driver confirms an
  amount within the limits (BR-P22) and
  has no other pending top-up
end note
pending --> credited : payment confirmed\n[valid, amount matches, not yet applied]\n/ credit full amount, settle shortfall,\nredeem points, request e-invoice
pending --> failed : payment failed\nor Driver cancels
pending --> c1 : at(next_attempt_at)\n[expires_at + 2, 15, 30, 45, 60 min;\n+75 min only if the 60-min query is RC 94]\n/ query gateway (querydr)
c1 --> credited : [paid]\n/ credit, as above
c1 --> pending : [answer unclear and slots left]\n/ set next_attempt_at
c1 --> expired : [not paid, or no slot left,\nor 5 failed attempts in a row]\n/ set exception_kind, tell Driver (MSG26)
expired --> [*]
credited --> refunded : Admin refunds it\n[balance ≥ amount]\n/ debit credit, restore points,\ncreate refund (STM-10)
failed --> [*]
refunded --> [*]
note right of c1
  exception_kind on expired:
  unresolved_04 / unresolved_07 = last
  gateway status 04 / 07 when the schedule ends;
  retry_exhausted = claim limit of 5 used up
  (listed for the Admin on Billing Exceptions)
end note
note bottom of expired
  Expiry is final. A payment confirmed after
  expiry is recorded as a late payment (no credit,
  no invoice), the top-up stays expired, and it is
  listed for Admin refund (STM-10, late_payment).
  A repeated payment result never changes the state.
end note
note bottom of failed
  A payment confirmed after failed is recorded the
  same way: late payment, the top-up stays failed.
end note
@enduml
